pages={
'Home':('# P2P Off-Ramp Wiki\n\nUnpublished local engineering draft. Trading is disabled; no approved release or deployment is implied. Never send real funds based on this wiki.\n\n[Getting Started](Getting-Started.md) · [Wallet and QR Safety](Wallet-and-QR-Safety.md) · [Privacy and Recovery](Privacy-and-Recovery.md) · [Security and Release](Security-and-Release.md) · [Architecture and Development](Architecture-and-Development.md) · [Codespaces Test Lab](Codespaces-Test-Lab.md)\n'),
'Getting-Started':('# Getting started\n\nImplemented local preview: create an encrypted profile, unlock/lock, inspect opaque inventory, export an explicitly unchecked encrypted backup, and restore to a separate fresh-key profile. Check recovery before relying on a backup. Origin changes may isolate browser storage.\n\nOffline review is available with an explicitly loaded synthetic demo registry. Checking terms is not acceptance, funding or fiat proof. The default build has no approved release key. Local Anvil tests use public development keys and cannot qualify a network deployment.\n\nManual settlement: seller alone releases before expiry after confirming fiat receipt; at or after expiry refund goes to the stored seller. A dishonest seller may withhold release after receiving fiat. Screenshots, chat, buyer assertions and bank notifications do not guarantee irreversible fiat settlement. Review network fees, token decimals, deadlines and full addresses. Protocol fees must never be inferred from a price example.\n\nNever disclose a seed phrase to a website, QR form or support contact. [Recovery](Privacy-and-Recovery.md) and [wallet safety](Wallet-and-QR-Safety.md).\n'),
'Privacy-and-Recovery':('# Privacy, encryption and recovery\n\nImplemented local vault records are encrypted using native WebCrypto AES-GCM with passphrase-derived key wrapping. Local tests cover authentication failures, corruption, concurrent writes and fresh-key recovery. This is scoped local evidence, not independent cryptographic approval. Unlocked origin code, extensions, weak passphrases and the OS can expose content.\n\nMessage-content encryption has vector and local test evidence; relay metadata, recipient copies and public advertisements remain separate. No browser-wide private routing is inferred from encryption or connectivity. Public chains expose transaction metadata. Selected route indicators must reflect current broker evidence; unknown wallet routing remains unknown. Stealth, location privacy and physical erasure are unsupported release claims.\n\nSaved reviews include private payment instructions; deletion is logical and does not erase backups or browser/OS remnants. Local backup-verification authenticates the current encrypted record set at a fixed profile/revision during the current unlocked session. It authenticates only the file supplied for this check against that profile revision. It does not execute a restore or authorize transactions. Cross-tab changes are detected on explicit recheck; the displayed result is point-in-time. Exported files still require their own recovery check. Restore writes a distinct fresh-key profile and retains the source. Restored identities require explicit consumer adoption; pending transactions require native reconciliation. Unknown broadcasts must not be blindly resent. [Release and incidents](Security-and-Release.md).\n'),
'Wallet-and-QR-Safety':('# Wallet and QR safety\n\nExternal wallets retain spending keys. Compare exact origin, network, full address, token, allowance, amount and expiry before wallet confirmation. Never enter wallet seeds or private keys into this app or support chat. QR/file interchange transports untrusted data; it does not authenticate a counterparty or payment. Preview and validate imported payloads before any action. Camera and device interoperability remain separately qualified.\n\nChain identity and deployed runtime must match the selected signed registry before enabled trading. A same-host checksum or a public URL does not authenticate initial application code. Default key pins remain unset; no deployment address is approved here. [Security and release](Security-and-Release.md).\n'),
'Architecture-and-Development':('# Architecture and developer setup\n\nImplemented architecture is a static React/TypeScript/Vite client with native Worker boundaries, encrypted IndexedDB, domain authority separation and external-wallet interfaces. Local EVM/relay/message test modules do not enable trading in the default artifact. There is no mandatory app-owned account server or server-held spending key.\n\nRun the commands in the [operator guide](../OPERATOR.md) and consult [development status](../DEVELOPMENT_STATUS.md). Specifications and structural audits are design/consistency evidence, not semantic acceptance. Preserve exact source revisions, dependency locks, protocol vectors, source licenses and asset digests. Accessibility, localization and mobile behavior need their recorded target matrix; local pseudo-locale checks do not prove WCAG or physical-device acceptance.\n'),
'Codespaces-Test-Lab':('# Codespaces test lab\n\nLocal native browser and Anvil harnesses exercise synthetic flows and fault cases. Use only published disposable development keys, never production seeds or funded accounts. Do not expose a local RPC port publicly. A cloud test environment does not establish device security or deployment readiness.\n\nA pinned linux/amd64 Node, Foundry and solc devcontainer recipe and fixed foundation/journey runner are implemented. Its local Docker build/tool and foundation checks are engineering evidence; no fresh Codespace or fresh npm-install qualification is implied. See the [lab recipe](../lab/README.md). Wiki hosting and independent Codespaces acceptance remain pending; this document does not claim a Codespace was provisioned. Browser emulation does not replace physical iOS/Android trials. [Developer setup](Architecture-and-Development.md).\n'),
'Security-and-Release':('# Security and release verification\n\nNo approved release, independent professional audit or maintained deployment is claimed. Default trading and network allowlists remain disabled. A signed manifest binds assets only under an actually selected trusted key; initial host/bootstrap trust remains separate. Check exact runtime identity, immutable escrow version and release provenance before any future enabled network flow.\n\nNo-script recovery instructions cannot decrypt a vault, sign, use a wallet, open a camera or prove current chain state. Use the supported recovery tool only after its trust prerequisites; never invent a downloadable approved binary from a source hash.\n\nOn conflicting native observations, unknown broadcast or compromised origin, stop economic actions, lock and preserve encrypted source data. Reconcile account/nonce and native finality before any explicit successor; never clear uncertainty because time passed. Report fixed error codes and public synthetic steps, not keys, payment instructions, raw provider errors or credentialed RPC URLs. Support must never request seeds. [Recovery](Privacy-and-Recovery.md).\n')}
for name,text in pages.items():(root/f'docs/wiki-source/{name}.md').write_text(text)
